---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What LexJolt collects: nothing you type. Here is the whole list.">
  <div class="lexjolt-shell lj-page" style="max-width:760px">
    <p class="lexjolt-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="lexjolt-h1">Nothing you type leaves the page</h1>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      The calculators are client-side code. Your inputs are read by the browser, the answer is computed
      in the browser, and nothing is submitted to a server. There is no account to delete because there
      is no account.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:28px">What is collected</h2>
    <ul class="lj-list">
      <li><b>Aggregate page views</b><span class="lj-sub">If analytics is enabled, a cookieless counter records the page path and referrer host — no cookies, no cross-site identifier, no fingerprint.</span></li>
      <li><b>Server logs</b><span class="lj-sub">The static host keeps standard request logs (IP, path, user agent) for a short retention window, as every host does.</span></li>
      <li><b>Nothing else</b><span class="lj-sub">No emails, no accounts, no advertising pixels, no third-party trackers on the calculator pages.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:28px">Shared links</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      When you change an input, the page rewrites its own URL with those values so you can send the
      calculation to someone. That is the only reason the numbers appear in the address bar; they are
      not logged by us beyond the ordinary request log, and they are not tied to you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:28px">The videos</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">
      The videos are static files served from this domain. Watching one does not load a third-party
      player or set an advertising cookie.
    </p>

    <h2 class="lexjolt-h2" style="margin-top:28px">Contact</h2>
    <p class="lj-lede-sm">Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
